All code in this repository is original, except:

1. kit/ — dgx-spark-recipe-kit (BHCC2025, Apache-2.0), vendored at a tagged release via git subtree. It includes the
   shared benchmark and smoke test that bench/bench.sh and scripts/smoke-test.sh run.

There are no patches and no vendored third-party code: TensorFold is installed from upstream, unmodified.

The engine is not part of this repository. docker/Dockerfile installs TensorFold (https://github.com/ashhart/TensorFold,
by @ashhart, Apache-2.0) from upstream at v0.6.2 (commit 56e2e3ec55bc0ae1d7d5158c4fa2c79a3567ab21), unmodified, into
NVIDIA's PyTorch container (nvcr.io/nvidia/pytorch:26.07-py3, governed by NVIDIA's software licence terms, which the
container prints when it starts).

This repository contains no model weights. ./setup.sh downloads, from Hugging Face and under its own licence
(Apache-2.0):
- TensorFold/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-MLX-4bit-MTP (formerly Vontra/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-MLX-4bit-MTP): Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B by the
  Qwen team, as mlx-community's MLX 4-bit conversion (mlx-community/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-4bit) plus the model's MTP layer
  converted the same way by the checkpoint's publisher.

The serve settings follow TensorFold's docs/recipes/qwen3.6-moe.md. The concurrency test runs TensorFold's
tools/bench_concurrent.py from the installed checkout; it is not copied here.
